Expert developer. English only.

# Cursor Efficiency (Token Optimization)
- Search: Use `grep` for exact matches/symbols, `codebase_search` for semantic queries only. Always specify `target_directories` to limit scope.
- Read files in parallel batches when possible. Read only necessary sections (offset/limit), not entire files.
- Be direct: Ask specific questions. Avoid exploratory searches. Use file paths from context when available.
- Tool selection: Prefer faster tools (grep > glob > codebase_search). Read files only when editing or critical.

# Code Style
- No comments, no docs. Self-explanatory code only. Functions=verbs, variables=nouns. No abbreviations. Never create README/docs files unless explicitly requested.
- Functions: Single responsibility, 20-40 lines. Max 3-4 params (use objects). Early returns, nesting ≤2.
- Types: Explicit public APIs. Validate at boundaries. Prefer immutability. Never swallow errors.

# Architecture
- Files: 200-400 lines (split if >400). Single responsibility. Exports: 1-3 related entities.
- Layers: UI (components) → domain (services/flows) → data/infrastructure.
- Imports: Standard → Third-party → Internal (@/*).

# Git
- Workflow: `feature/`, `bugfix/`, `hotfix/`, `release/vX.Y.Z`. Protected: `main`, `develop` (PRs required). CRITICAL: Verify branch first.
- Commits: `<gitmoji> <intent>: <description>` + bullet points. ✨🐛♻️💄🎨⚡🔥📝🚀🔒🚧📦

# Testing (Vitest)
- Run `npm run test:ci` before commits. Test non-trivial logic (Arrange/Act/Assert). Fast, isolated.
- Before review: `npm run test:ci` + `coderabbit --prompt-only -t uncommitted`.

# Stack
Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind + Shadcn UI, Firebase (Auth/Firestore), OpenRouter, React Context/Hooks

# CodeRabbit
`coderabbit --prompt-only -t uncommitted` (max 3 runs). Help: `cr -h`
